{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Eightfold.IndecomposableQuotientPrune","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Eightfold.IndecomposableQuotientPrune","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Module.Submodule.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Span.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.IndecomposableQuotient.unit_smul_eq_self","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.IndecomposableQuotient.unit_smul_eq_self","kind":"theorem","line":165,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/IndecomposableQuotientPrune.lean#L165-L173","doc":"**And the action is trivial when the degree-0 stratum is the unit.**\n\nThe corpus's own `ℋ_q^(0,K)` is the central idempotent `e_{λ_K}` (or scalars,\nper `def:hq-bi-filtration`'s low-`(n,K)` grid), and `ℋ_q^(2,K)` is the\n`e_K`-isotypic piece — so the acting element **is** the unit of the localised\nalgebra `e_K ℋ_q e_K`, and acts as the identity. That is route A's action,\nexisting and doing nothing. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.IndecomposableQuotient.mkQ_smul_mul_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.IndecomposableQuotient.mkQ_smul_mul_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":153,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/IndecomposableQuotientPrune.lean#L153-L159","doc":"**The action descends to the indecomposable quotient**, on generators: a\ndegree-0 element acting on a product is still zero there. This is what route A\nneeds in order to act on the volume stratum at all. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.IndecomposableQuotient.smul_mul_mem_decomposable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.IndecomposableQuotient.smul_mul_mem_decomposable","kind":"theorem","line":144,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/IndecomposableQuotientPrune.lean#L144-L151","doc":"**A product stays decomposable after acting by a degree-0 element.**\nHypothesis `hcompat` is `c • mul a b = mul (c • a) b` — acting on a product is\nacting on its first factor, the `0 + 1 = 1` half of shuffle-additivity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.IndecomposableQuotient.decomposable_zero_eq_bot","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.IndecomposableQuotient.decomposable_zero_eq_bot","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/IndecomposableQuotientPrune.lean#L93-L102","doc":"**Non-vacuity.** The prune is not true merely because the quotient collapses:\nfor the zero multiplication the decomposable part is `⊥`, so the quotient is all\nof `A₂` and is nontrivial whenever `A₂` is. The theorem therefore has content\nabout *which* elements die, not about everything dying. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.IndecomposableQuotient.mkQ_eq_zero_of_mem_decomposable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.IndecomposableQuotient.mkQ_eq_zero_of_mem_decomposable","kind":"theorem","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/IndecomposableQuotientPrune.lean#L87-L91","doc":"The same for an arbitrary element of the decomposable part: the whole image\nof the multiplication is killed, not just its generators. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.IndecomposableQuotient.mkQ_mul_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.IndecomposableQuotient.mkQ_mul_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/IndecomposableQuotientPrune.lean#L77-L85","doc":"**The prune.** In the indecomposable quotient `A₂ ⧸ decomposable`, every\nproduct of two degree-1 elements is **zero**.\n\nRead on the corpus's dictionary: a shuffle-square of depth-1 elements is zero in\nthe part of weight 2 that `K_3^ind` — and hence the hyperbolic volume — lives\nin. Squaring cannot reach an indecomposable target. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.IndecomposableQuotient.mul_mem_decomposable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.IndecomposableQuotient.mul_mem_decomposable","kind":"theorem","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/IndecomposableQuotientPrune.lean#L72-L75","doc":"Every product of two degree-1 elements is decomposable. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.IndecomposableQuotient.decomposable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.IndecomposableQuotient.decomposable","kind":"def","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/IndecomposableQuotientPrune.lean#L66-L70","doc":"The **decomposable** submodule of the degree-2 piece: the span of all\nproducts of two degree-1 elements. This is the object the `ind` qualifier\nquotients by. ","signatureChunk":0}]}